"""
Straight-line runs of the planar car on the 2 % ramp road, steering wheel held straight by
`column`, no drive: a coast up the ramp and a braked stop with load transfer on the level road.
The car's road load reads the grade from a `RoadGrade` under the chassis; the assertions read
the car's own bus. The model holds the planar `World`, gravity off. It has no ports.

The car is the default `Body.Planar.Car` of `m` = 1500 kg with its CG `h_cg` = 0.55 m above the
road and load transfer on. Each case starts on the road's center line, heading along x, at
25 m/s with every wheel rolling at 25/0.31 rad/s, from x = `x0`.

`ramp_z.crg` climbs at exactly 2 % on 0 to 500 m (`Body.Planar.Tests.RoadGrade` derives it).
Before its grid starts at x = 0 the road blends over 2 m to height 0 and is level below -2 m,
so its slope there is exactly 0.

- `climb` starts at x = 10 m and stays on the 2 % ramp, so tan(alpha) = 0.02,
  cos(alpha) = 1/sqrt(1.0004) = 0.99980006 and sin(alpha) = 0.01999600.
- `braking` starts at x = -300 m, on the level road, with 250 N m on every brake. The brakes are
  `Chassis.Wheel.BrakeActuator`s on the car's wheel shafts, each reacting on its own mount, and
  `brake.k` is each one's request; the other cases request 0.
- `reverse` checks only the start of a car driving backward and sliding left, at
  vx = -19.363634 m/s and vy = 6.503820 m/s: the bus reads
  beta = atan(6.503820/max(|-19.363634|, 1)) = 0.324039 rad, where a sideslip taken against vx
  would read atan(6.503820) = 1.418235 rad.

The wheels turn with the chassis, so the four wheel inertias add J/r² each to the mass the
forces decelerate: m_eff = 1500 + 4 · 1/0.31² = 1541.6233 kg. Coasting, the tires slip only the
few mm/s that spin the wheels down, so the car follows m_eff dv/dt = -(c v² + A) with
c = rho CdA/2 = 0.378 kg/m and A the speed-independent part of the force:

- climb: A = m g (f_r cos(alpha) + sin(alpha)) = 14709.975 · (0.0119976 + 0.0199960) =
  470.6251 N;
- braking: on the level road the rolling resistance is f_r m g = 0.012 · 1500 · 9.80665 =
  176.5197 N, and with the brakes A = 176.5197 + 4 · 250/0.31 = 176.5197 + 3225.8065 =
  3402.3262 N once the brakes' 0.03 s actuator lag has passed. The lag delivers the brake force's
  full impulse 0.03 s late, so the run is the unbraked coast (A = 176.5197 N, s = 21.609797 m/s,
  k = 0.0052986 1/s) for 0.03 s followed by the braked law for 1.97 s; the drag's
  change over the lag is below 1e-4 m/s.

With s = sqrt(A/c), k = sqrt(A c)/m_eff and theta0 = atan(v0/s), the speed is
v(t) = s tan(theta0 - k t) and the distance (m_eff/c) ln(cos(theta0 - k t)/cos(theta0)):

- climb, 10 s: s = 35.285123 m/s, k = 0.0086518 1/s, theta0 = 0.616417, v = 20.669387 m/s
  after 227.943473 m, so x = 237.943473 m;
- braking, 2 s: the unbraked coast's first 0.03 s ends at 24.991969 m/s after 0.749880 m; then
  s = 94.872877 m/s, k = 0.0232625 1/s and theta0 = atan(24.991969/s) = 0.257574 give
  20.394800 m/s after another 44.689427 m, at -(0.378 · 20.394800² + 3402.3262)/1541.6233 =
  -2.308965 m/s².

Braking, the tires carry the brake torque at a slip that is not small. Each wheel's tire force is
F = T/r + J a/r² = 806.45 - 24.03 = 782.42 N (the wheel decelerates with the car), and its
longitudinal slip speed v_sl solves F = F_z c(x) with x = v_sl/(s_A (v - v_sl)), s_A = 0.12
front and 0.09 rear; with the loads below, x = 0.118049 front and 0.180846 rear, so
v_sl = 0.284891 m/s front and 0.326641 m/s rear. The wheels spin that much slower than rolling,
so the car keeps the wheels' missing angular momentum: its speed is higher by
J Σv_sl/(r² m_eff) = 1 · 1.223064/(0.0961 · 1541.6233) = 0.008256 m/s, v = 20.403056 m/s. The
slip shrinks with the speed (v_sl ∝ v at a constant force), which adds J Σv_sl a/(v r² m_eff) =
-0.000935 m/s² to the acceleration, a = -2.309900 m/s², and over the braking phase the speed
offset adds 0.008256 · 44.689427/20.394800 = 0.018091 m to the distance, x = -254.542602 m.
The car's bus reads the wheels' slip ratio (r w - v)/v = -v_sl/v: -0.284891/20.403056 =
-0.013963 front and -0.326641/20.403056 = -0.016009 rear, and their spin speeds
(v - v_sl)/r: (20.403056 - 0.284891)/0.31 = 64.8973 rad/s front and 64.7626 rad/s rear.

The braked case's wheel loads: at rest each front wheel carries m g b/(2 L) = 4086.1042 N and
each rear wheel m g a/(2 L) = 3268.8833 N (a = 1.2 m, b = 1.5 m, L = 2.7 m). The loads see the
acceleration through the 0.05 s suspension lag, which trails a ramp of slope
da/dt = -2 c v a/m_eff = 0.023093 m/s³ by 0.05 · 0.023093 = 0.001155 m/s², so they see
-2.311055 m/s² and move m · 2.311055 · 0.55/(2 · 2.7) = 353.0778 N onto each front wheel:
4439.1820 N front and 2915.8055 N rear.

Straight ahead on a level-across road with equal loads left and right, nothing turns the car: it
keeps y = 0 and no yaw rate. The straight run is neutrally stable sideways, so rounding drifts y
by up to about 1e-5 m over the run, which its tolerance allows.
"""
test component PlanarCoast
  "Start position of the chassis along the road's center line"
  parameter x0::Length = -300.0
  "Start speed of the chassis along its heading"
  parameter vx0::Velocity = 25.0
  "Start speed of the chassis to its left"
  parameter vy0::Velocity = 0.0
  car = VehicleComponents.Body.Planar.Car(h_cg = 0.55, load_transfer = true, body(r = initial [x0, 0.0], v = initial [vx0, vy0]), fl(inertia(w = initial vx0 / 0.31)), fr(inertia(w = initial vx0 / 0.31)), rl(inertia(w = initial vx0 / 0.31)), rr(inertia(w = initial vx0 / 0.31))) {^car}
  road = VehicleComponents.Body.Planar.RoadGrade(road = VehicleComponents.Road.slope("dyad://VehicleComponents/data/roads/ramp_z.crg")) {^road}
  "Rolling resistance coefficient, a car tire on asphalt"
  tire = BlockComponents.Sources.Constant(k = 0.012) {^tire}
  "Holds the steering wheel straight"
  column = RotationalComponents.Components.Fixed() {^column}
  "Brake request on every wheel"
  brake = BlockComponents.Sources.Constant(k = 0.0) {^brake}
  actuator_fl = VehicleComponents.Chassis.Wheel.BrakeActuator(tau_max = 2500.0) {^actuator_fl}
  actuator_fr = VehicleComponents.Chassis.Wheel.BrakeActuator(tau_max = 2500.0) {^actuator_fr}
  actuator_rl = VehicleComponents.Chassis.Wheel.BrakeActuator(tau_max = 2500.0) {^actuator_rl}
  actuator_rr = VehicleComponents.Chassis.Wheel.BrakeActuator(tau_max = 2500.0) {^actuator_rr}
  mount_fl = RotationalComponents.Components.Fixed() {^mount_fl}
  mount_fr = RotationalComponents.Components.Fixed() {^mount_fr}
  mount_rl = RotationalComponents.Components.Fixed() {^mount_rl}
  mount_rr = RotationalComponents.Components.Fixed() {^mount_rr}
  "Planar world with its gravity off: the car lies in the road plane"
  world = MultibodyComponents.PlanarMechanics.World(g = 0.0) {^world}
relations
  connect(car.chassis, road.frame_a) {^id7}
  connect(road.grade, car.grade) {^id8}
  connect(tire.y, car.f_r) {^id9}
  connect(column.spline, car.steering) {^id10}
  connect(brake.y, actuator_fl.tau_cmd, actuator_rl.tau_cmd, actuator_fr.tau_cmd, actuator_rr.tau_cmd) {^id11}
  connect(car.spin_fl, actuator_fl.spline_b) {^b1}
  connect(car.spin_fr, actuator_fr.spline_a) {^b2}
  connect(car.spin_rl, actuator_rl.spline_b) {^b3}
  connect(car.spin_rr, actuator_rr.spline_a) {^b4}
  connect(actuator_fl.support, mount_fl.spline) {^b5}
  connect(actuator_fr.support, mount_fr.spline) {^b6}
  connect(actuator_rl.support, mount_rl.spline) {^b7}
  connect(actuator_rr.support, mount_rr.spline) {^b8}
metadata {
  "Dyad": {
    "tests": {
      "climb": {
        "stop": 10,
        "solver": "Auto",
        "abstol": 1e-7,
        "reltol": 1e-7,
        "params": {"x0": 10.0},
        "atol": {"car.bus.vx": 0.001, "car.bus.x": 0.01, "car.bus.y": 0.001, "car.bus.r": 1e-6},
        "expect": {
          "initial": {"car.bus.vx": 25.0, "car.bus.x": 10.0},
          "final": {
            "car.bus.vx": 20.669387,
            "car.bus.x": 237.943473,
            "car.bus.y": 0.0,
            "car.bus.r": 0.0
          }
        }
      },
      "reverse": {
        "stop": 0.01,
        "solver": "Auto",
        "abstol": 1e-7,
        "reltol": 1e-7,
        "params": {"vx0": -19.363634, "vy0": 6.50382},
        "atol": {"car.bus.vx": 1e-6, "car.bus.beta": 1e-6},
        "expect": {"initial": {"car.bus.vx": -19.363634, "car.bus.beta": 0.324039}}
      },
      "braking": {
        "stop": 2,
        "solver": "Auto",
        "abstol": 1e-7,
        "reltol": 1e-7,
        "params": {"brake.k": 250.0},
        "atol": {
          "car.bus.vx": 0.002,
          "car.bus.x": 0.01,
          "car.bus.ax": 0.001,
          "car.fl.F_z": 0.5,
          "car.fr.F_z": 0.5,
          "car.rl.F_z": 0.5,
          "car.rr.F_z": 0.5,
          "car.bus.y": 0.001,
          "car.bus.r": 1e-6,
          "car.bus.kappa_fl": 0.0005,
          "car.bus.kappa_fr": 0.0005,
          "car.bus.kappa_rl": 0.0005,
          "car.bus.kappa_rr": 0.0005,
          "car.bus.omega_fl": 0.01,
          "car.bus.omega_rl": 0.01
        },
        "expect": {
          "initial": {"car.bus.vx": 25.0, "car.bus.x": -300.0},
          "final": {
            "car.bus.vx": 20.403056,
            "car.bus.x": -254.542602,
            "car.bus.ax": -2.309900,
            "car.fl.F_z": 4439.1820,
            "car.fr.F_z": 4439.1820,
            "car.rl.F_z": 2915.8055,
            "car.rr.F_z": 2915.8055,
            "car.bus.y": 0.0,
            "car.bus.r": 0.0,
            "car.bus.kappa_fl": -0.013963,
            "car.bus.kappa_fr": -0.013963,
            "car.bus.kappa_rl": -0.016009,
            "car.bus.kappa_rr": -0.016009,
            "car.bus.omega_fl": 64.8973,
            "car.bus.omega_rl": 64.7626
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "_links": {
